# p_61d5 — Elena's morning: bathroom shelf by 7, laptop and bag at the entry by 8

Elena is up by 6:15. She moves her toiletry bag from the dresser to the bathroom shelf (sighted there 5 times at 07:00), takes a shower using her towel from the same shelf (4 sightings at 07:00, 4 at 08:00), and dries her hair with the hair dryer that lives permanently on the bathroom shelf (11 sightings, 5/5 days). By 07:30 she has packed her laptop into her backpack; both are at the entry hook by 08:00, ready for her commute. The laptop is sighted at entry_hook_e1 at 03:00 (× 2) the previous night and at coffee_table_l1 at 18:00 the evening before—so it cycles: coffee table in the evening → entry hook overnight → out the door by 08:00.

What sets this apart: p_d9e1 covers the toiletry bag at 6:5–7:5 but also claims the hair dryer is at the bathroom shelf at 9–12 h (which went against 1×). This document keeps the hair dryer at the shelf all day (it is a fixed item, 5/5 days) and narrows the toiletry bag window to 06:30–08:00, after which the bag goes back to the dresser (sighted at dresser at 18:00). The laptop at the entry hook in the 07–08 h window is a distinct prediction: p_a1b2 and p_c3d4 place it at the desk or out of the house during 9–17 h but do not pin its pre-departure location.

Refutation: if the toiletry bag is found on the dresser (not the bathroom shelf) at 07:00 on two or more weekday mornings, or if the laptop is sighted at the coffee table or desk (not the entry hook) during 07:00–08:00 on a weekday, the morning sequence is wrong.

